          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "নাগরদোলা (nāgôrdolā) is usually explained as নাগর, 'of the town' — Sanskrit nāgara, 'town-born' (Monier-Williams) — with দোলা, a swing, the word behind দোলানো (CDIAL 6453): the great swing of the fair."
            }
          ]
        },
